e of personal assets or new family-business divestment.\n- 7B.4 (family enrichment): the offshore-history pre-2023 facts remain the relevant context; no 2023 event contradicts or supersedes them.\n- 7B.5 (competent appointments vs loyalists): WEB-014R documents the loyalist pattern.\n- 7B.6 (independent investigation): 2023 raids on Mintz, Bain, Franklin Templeton/BlackRock, and the Liu Siwei/Yang Zewei/Anna Kwok family arrests (HRW 2024) document the squeeze.\n- 7B.7 (concealment): the Counter-Espionage Law amendment plus raids plus transnational repression.\n- 7B.8 (promises): the public record in 2023 is mixed; common-prosperity redirection and zero-Covid reversal are not broken promises in the formal sense.\n- 7B.9 (nepotism/favoritism): the loyalist pattern (WEB-014R) is the principal 7B.9 evidence.\n- 7B.10 (ethical example): the loyalist-appointment pattern, the suppression of independent investigation, and the offshore-network precedent all inform 7B.10.\n\n**Source mix (7B):** V-Dem/CPI (local), PRC Leader, HRW, Amnesty, BBC, RSF, DOJ. Seven independent source families.\n\n**Adjudication calibration note for 7B:** The reviewer flagged that the chapter is genuinely thin. The 7B evidence is dominated by counter-espionage, raids, and loyalist appointments. There is no traceable 2023 personal disclosure, family-enrichment, or nepotism event. The 7B defensible count is conservative: WEB-014R (loyalist appointments), WEB-009R (law and raids), WEB-026R (DOJ indictments), WEB-008R (system pattern). Four defensible items; the chapter should be flagged for confidence limits.\n\n## 8B Effectiveness and Competence\n\n**Exposure/program:** Mostly explicit. The 2023 NDRC implementation report provides the official program implementation record.\n\n**Defensible evidence (final_evidence):**\n\n- WEB-013R (NDRC 2023 Plan Implementation): 5.2% GDP growth, 12.44M urban jobs, 5.2% unemployment, R&D +8.1%, NEV +30%, 4.015M patents, 6,067 private-investment projects. **8B.2, 8B.6, 8B.7, 8B.10**.\n- WEB-015R (PRC Leader 1 Mar 2023 zero-Covid exit): reversal of signature policy. **8B.1, 8B.2, 8B.5, 8B.8**.\n- WEB-014R (PRC Leader 6 Jun 2023 economic team + reorganization): named officials; central commissions in finance, S&T; party takeover of Hong Kong/Macao. **8B.1, 8B.2, 8B.3, 8B.4, 8B.5**.\n- WEB-016R (BBC 15 Aug 2023): youth-unemployment data suspension, PBOC rate cut. **8B.6, 8B.7, 8B.8**.\n- WEB-017R (Guardian 18 Aug 2023): property sector default rate 40% since 2020; rate cut; deflation. **8B.6, 8B.7, 8B.8, 8B.9**.\n- WEB-023R (PRC Leader 1 Mar 2023): no 2023 redistribution policy. **8B.2, 8B.6, 8B.7, 8B.8**.\n- WEB-005aR (BBC Nov 16 2023): Xi–Biden restored mil-to-mil and presidential hotline. **8B.9**.\n- WEB-005bR (BBC Nov 16 2023): AI dialogue, fentanyl commitments, Taiwan as \"most dangerous issue.\" **8B.9**.\n- WEB-001R (FAS): 500-warhead arsenal, rapid modernization, NFU reaffirmed. **8B.2, 8B.3, 8B.6, 8B.7**.\n- WEB-029R (Beijing Work Report 15 Jan 2023): \"all localities working under Xi\" — political-coordination implementation. **8B.5**.\n- WEB-011R (HRW Xi's August 2023 Xinjiang visit \"success\" claim). **8B.6, 8B.7, 8B.9**.\n\n**Sparse lens notes:**\n\n- 8B.1 (program clarity): clearly explicit and consistent across multiple official texts.\n- 8B.2 (translation into plans/budgets/appointments): the 2023 Government Work Report (Li Keqiang) and the 2023 Plan Implementation (NDRC) are the main program-conversion documents.\n- 8B.3 (mobilization): partial success in installing loyalists; mixed in economic implementation.\n- 8B.4 (personnel fit): PRC Leader's piece raises a question of whether loyalists are also competent. The IMF Article IV and HRW note a tension between political control and professionalization. **8B.4, 8B.5**.\n- 8B.5 (internal coordination): the year-end pivot from zero-Covid to growth, the property handling, and the youth-unemployment data suspension suggest mixed coordination.\n- 8B.6 (declarations into implementation): the apparent absence of redistribution policy (WEB-023R) is a clear case of implementation gap.\n- 8B.7 (outcomes move as claimed): mixed; growth held near target, but property, youth unemployment, and stock-market confidence all worsened; common-prosperity indicators (Gini, fiscal progressivity) did not move.\n- 8B.8 (adaptation): the zero-Covid exit is the headline adaptation; the loyalist economic team replacing the more technocratic Li Keqiang era is the headline re-purposing.\n- 8B.9 (crisis management): mil-to-mil restoration, fentanyl agreement, AI dialogue, and the November arms-control consultation are concrete crisis-management moves; the property and youth crises are not yet resolved in 2023.\n- 8B.10 (durable progress): mixed; loyalty-based rule is now durable, but economic dynamism and social welfare did not advance.\n\n**Source mix (8B):** NDRC (official), PRC Leader (specialized), BBC, Guardian, FAS, ACA, RSF, HRW, Beijing Municipal Government, BBC mil-to-mil. Ten independent source families.\n\n---\n\n# 3. Cross-chapter reuse and same-URL splits\n\n| URL/web ID | Used by chapters |\n|---|---|\n| WEB-001R (FAS Nuclear Notebook) | 1B, 2B (context), 8B |\n| WEB-002R (FAS/Bloomberg) | 1B (context), 7B (context), 8B (context) |\n| WEB-003R (ACA Nov 6 2023 meeting) | 1B, 2B |\n| WEB-004R (ACA Xi–Biden follow-up) | 1B, 2B |\n| WEB-005aR (BBC mil-to-mil) | 1B, 2B, 8B |\n| WEB-005bR (BBC AI/Taiwan/fentanyl) | 2B, 8B |\n| WEB-005cR (BBC \"dictator\" remark) | 4B |\n| WEB-006R (HRW Russia/Assad) | 2B |\n| WEB-007R (HRW GSI/GDI/GCI/DOJ) | 2B, 3B |\n| WEB-008R (HRW named individuals, Hong Kong) | 3B, 4B, 7B |\n| WEB-009R (HRW Caixin, Counter-espionage, UFLPA, Li Keqiang) | 3B, 4B, 6B, 7B |\n| WEB-010R (HRW Jan 2024 press release) | 3B, 4B |\n| WEB-011R (HRW Xi Xinjiang visit) | 3B, 4B, 8B |\n| WEB-012R (RSF Yang Zewei) | 3B, 4B, 7B |\n| WEB-013R (NDRC 2023 Plan Implementation) | 5B, 6B, 8B |\n| WEB-014R (PRC Leader economic team) | 4B, 7B, 8B 